  "id": "atlanta",
  "intro": "Atlanta is defined by one thing on the air: Hartsfield-Jackson is the busiest airport in the world, and has been for most of the last thirty years. The approach and departure sectors are working continuously in a way no other American field matches, and from the north side of town you can sit and listen to a landing every forty seconds. Beyond the airport, this is a hilly, heavily wooded metro where UHF struggles, and a huge inland rail hub built where four railroads once met.",
  "introz": "亚特兰大在频谱上只被一件事定义：哈兹菲尔德—杰克逊是全球最繁忙的机场，过去三十年里大部分时间都是。它的进离场扇区的繁忙程度是美国任何其他机场都比不了的，在城北能坐下来听着大约每四十秒一次的落地。除机场之外，这是一个多丘陵、林木茂密的都会区，UHF 传播吃力；它同时也是一个巨大的内陆铁路枢纽，当年由四条铁路交汇而成。",
